commit 877fd0f631cb2a2c2a1902e265be24eb6cc0eb42
Author: Andrea Pari <56761212+pariandrea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Jun 11 19:36:33 2026 +0100

    feat(Mathematics/Calculus): Wirtinger calculus foundation with directional operators and Schwarz's theorem (#1163)
    
    * feat(Mathematics/Calculus): Wirtinger algebraic foundation (Basic.lean)
    
    Basic.lean provides the algebraic input to the Wirtinger calculus: the
    real-linear Wirtinger decomposition of a map ℂ →L[ℝ] ℂ
    (realLinear_apply_eq_wirtinger), and the fact that differentiation
    commutes with conjugation, d f̄ = conj(d f) (fderiv_star_eq).
    
    Differentiating complex, non-holomorphic functions requires the
    Wirtinger derivatives ∂/∂φ and ∂/∂φ̄, which Mathlib does not provide.
    This foundation is essential for the ongoing SUSY formalisation.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * feat(Mathematics/Calculus): directional Wirtinger operators and Schwarz's theorem (Multivariable.lean)
    
    Multivariable.lean defines the directional Wirtinger operators ∂_v f,
    ∂̄_v f on f : V → ℂ over a complex vector space V, built on fderiv ℝ and
    the algebraic lemmas of Basic.lean: real-linearity, the Leibniz and
    finite-sum rules, inner-field conjugation, the two-term chain rule for an
    outer g : ℂ → ℂ, domain conjugation, the holomorphic/anti-holomorphic
    collapse, and differentiability and locality on a C² field. The capstone
    is Schwarz's theorem in Wirtinger form, ∂_v ∂̄_w f = ∂̄_w ∂_v f, reduced to
    ContDiffAt.isSymmSndFDerivAt.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * refactor(Mathematics/Calculus): merge Wirtinger calculus into a single Basic file
    
    Fold the two algebraic lemmas (realLinear_apply_eq_wirtinger, fderiv_star_eq)
    into the directional-calculus foundation, placing each in the section that
    consumes it (§C Conjugation, §D chain rule), and rename Multivariable.lean →
    Basic.lean — one foundation file, per review feedback. Drop the FDeriv.Comp and
    FDeriv.Linear imports now subsumed by FDeriv.Symmetric.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    * refactor(Mathematics/Calculus): make weightedDirDeriv the Wirtinger primitive
    
    Define weightedDirDeriv up front in §A and derive dWirtingerDir/dWirtingerAntiDir
    as its two specializations (c = ∓i), so the §G second-derivative bridge is
    definitional and the dWirtinger…_eq_weightedDirDeriv lemmas become rfl. Downstream
    proofs unfold via the explicit dWirtinger…_apply lemmas. Inline the trivial
    differentiableAt_fderiv helper at its three call sites. Addresses review comments.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
